1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:36,537 --> 00:01:40,667
Parti mis tuelo morow.

17
00:01:40,667 --> 00:01:43,557
Lu spinzzio tilatto cul.

18
00:01:52,797 --> 00:01:54,737
Thank you.

19
00:01:54,737 --> 00:01:56,927
Same to you.

20
00:01:58,587 --> 00:02:00,397
Thank you very much.

21
00:02:08,067 --> 00:02:08,987
Well, then...

22
00:02:08,987 --> 00:02:09,937
Um...

23
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:13,987
Where did you come to hear of this road?

24
00:02:13,987 --> 00:02:16,287
At a recent stop in a Poroson tavern.

25
00:02:16,287 --> 00:02:18,697
Didn't you hear the rumors about the wolves?

26
00:02:19,117 --> 00:02:20,967
I did indeed.

27
00:02:20,967 --> 00:02:24,087
But I'm in a hurry, so I decided to take the risk.

28
00:02:24,627 --> 00:02:26,047
I see...

29
00:02:29,147 --> 00:02:31,297
Is something the matter?

30
00:02:32,677 --> 00:02:34,847
No... I mean...

31
00:02:36,017 --> 00:02:39,507
Ask anything at all. Is there something you need?

32
00:02:41,147 --> 00:02:42,817
Is there any way

33
00:02:42,817 --> 00:02:44,517
that you could hire me?

34
00:02:47,777 --> 00:02:52,777
Wolf and the Shepherd's Lamb

35
00:02:53,627 --> 00:02:55,447
I'm a shepherd.

36
00:02:55,447 --> 00:02:59,157
I can stave off wolves as well as care for sheep.

37
00:02:59,157 --> 00:03:05,127
If you hire me, I can protect you from wolves during your journey.

38
00:03:05,127 --> 00:03:06,457
Would you consider it?

39
00:03:08,087 --> 00:03:09,167
Enek.

40
00:03:24,607 --> 00:03:27,777
Wait just a moment while I ask my companion.

41
00:03:28,227 --> 00:03:29,397
Her skills?

42
00:03:29,817 --> 00:03:33,567
If she's skilled, she might be worth hiring.

43
00:03:33,567 --> 00:03:35,177
You heard us, surely.

44
00:03:35,637 --> 00:03:37,867
You already have me, do you not?

45
00:03:38,237 --> 00:03:41,037
I know having you by my side is more than enough.

46
00:03:41,037 --> 00:03:45,617
But it's never occurred to me to use a shepherd to drive off wolves.

47
00:03:46,577 --> 00:03:49,077
There could be a new business in it.

48
00:03:49,957 --> 00:03:53,627
Human males like to have as many females as possible, it seems.

49
00:03:56,357 --> 00:03:58,297
I'm not being blinded by her charm.

50
00:03:58,717 --> 00:04:01,887
You're much cuter than her, anyway.

51
00:04:05,977 --> 00:04:08,797
I suppose that's a passing mark.

52
00:04:10,397 --> 00:04:12,277
So, what of her skill?

53
00:04:12,277 --> 00:04:14,657
I suppose she'd be in the high range.

54
00:04:14,657 --> 00:04:16,197
Be a little more concrete.

55
00:04:16,787 --> 00:04:19,827
I could take a sheep from her,

56
00:04:19,827 --> 00:04:24,417
but ordinary wolves wouldn't stand a chance, even in packs.

57
00:04:25,917 --> 00:04:27,077
Is that so?

58
00:04:27,077 --> 00:04:29,457
She's very skilled at handling her dog.

59
00:04:30,917 --> 00:04:36,547
The nastiest shepherds are the ones who have a clever dog that they share a strong bond with.

60
00:04:37,247 --> 00:04:39,757
It looks to me like both those things are true of her.

61
00:04:39,757 --> 00:04:43,047
Her voice suggests she's young, which means she'll get even nastier.

62
00:04:43,047 --> 00:04:46,177
Perhaps I should do something about that...

63
00:04:46,557 --> 00:04:48,507
All right, all right. Thanks.

64
00:04:48,937 --> 00:04:50,067
Wait.

65
00:04:51,397 --> 00:04:53,487
Are you really going to hire her?

66
00:04:54,317 --> 00:04:55,937
I was planning to.

67
00:04:57,657 --> 00:05:02,657
If you hire her, she will be accompanying us for a time, right?

68
00:05:03,697 --> 00:05:04,447
You don't want to?

69
00:05:04,787 --> 00:05:06,747
It's not that I do not want to.

70
00:05:08,327 --> 00:05:10,497
Lubinheigen's only two days away.

71
00:05:10,497 --> 00:05:11,497
Still no good?

72
00:05:12,047 --> 00:05:14,167
Nor did I say that.

73
00:05:14,627 --> 00:05:17,297
Sorry, but bear with it for a little while.

74
00:05:18,297 --> 00:05:20,637
What am I supposed to bear?

75
00:05:21,057 --> 00:05:22,217
Well, I mean...

76
00:05:23,057 --> 00:05:28,187
Really, I only want to see how effective a shepherd is against wolves.

77
00:05:28,187 --> 00:05:30,807
That's fine with me. <i>You're</i> the one who might have a problem.

78
00:05:31,687 --> 00:05:36,607
What will you do if my identity is exposed while she's traveling with us?

79
00:05:45,447 --> 00:05:46,787
I get it now.

80
00:05:47,577 --> 00:05:49,667
You wanted me to say something like...

81
00:05:51,367 --> 00:05:54,707
"I want to travel together, just the two of us."

82
00:05:56,167 --> 00:05:57,257
Fool!

83
00:05:57,257 --> 00:05:58,217
Sorry.

84
00:05:58,217 --> 00:05:59,207
Geez.

85
00:05:59,747 --> 00:06:02,597
Well, I doubt I'll be exposed in two days.

86
00:06:03,927 --> 00:06:05,467
Do as you will.

87
00:06:06,677 --> 00:06:08,347
Sorry to keep you waiting.

88
00:06:10,227 --> 00:06:11,397
Not at all!

89
00:06:11,397 --> 00:06:12,437
So...

90
00:06:12,437 --> 00:06:15,477
How does forty Trie for the trip to Lubinheigen sound?

91
00:06:15,897 --> 00:06:20,337
With a bonus if we happen to be attacked by wolves but make it unharmed.

92
00:06:22,157 --> 00:06:23,447
Is that not enough?

93
00:06:23,907 --> 00:06:26,727
It's perfect. Thank you very much!

94
00:06:27,247 --> 00:06:28,197
Likewise.

95
00:06:29,567 --> 00:06:32,077
May I inquire as to your name?

96
00:06:32,077 --> 00:06:33,787
Oh, I'm sorry.

97
00:06:34,377 --> 00:06:36,867
N-Norah Arendt.

98
00:06:46,887 --> 00:06:48,347
Enek!

99
00:06:56,727 --> 00:06:58,517
Have you been a shepherd long?

100
00:06:59,237 --> 00:07:01,947
No, just four years now.

101
00:07:01,947 --> 00:07:05,907
I began my time as a shepherd when I first met him.

102
00:07:05,907 --> 00:07:07,697
That's unusual.

103
00:07:07,697 --> 00:07:08,527
And before that?

104
00:07:10,957 --> 00:07:16,537
I helped at an almshouse attached to an abbey and in return was allowed to live there.

105
00:07:18,117 --> 00:07:23,297
While I was relying on the almshouse, I'd always wanted to find a real trade of my own.

106
00:07:23,887 --> 00:07:26,637
It was good fortune meeting Enek.

107
00:07:26,637 --> 00:07:28,547
Your prayers were surely answered.

108
00:07:29,057 --> 00:07:34,357
Yes, I can't help but think that I have God to thank for our meeting.

109
00:07:40,327 --> 00:07:43,907
When I found him, he was in a sad state, covered in wounds.

110
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:45,367
From wolves?

111
00:07:46,697 --> 00:07:50,117
No, probably from bandits or mercenaries.

112
00:07:50,117 --> 00:07:54,577
He was cowering under an overhang on a hill with this staff in his mouth.

113
00:07:54,577 --> 00:07:55,457
I see.

114
00:07:56,157 --> 00:08:00,627
I must say, I never would have expected you to offer to escort me.

115
00:08:01,217 --> 00:08:03,257
It's hardly a common thing for shepherds to do, is it?

116
00:08:05,217 --> 00:08:07,017
Well...

117
00:08:07,017 --> 00:08:08,387
I just

118
00:08:08,387 --> 00:08:09,767
wanted to talk to someone.

119
00:08:11,057 --> 00:08:12,557
I know that feeling.

120
00:08:12,557 --> 00:08:16,267
And I actually want to become a seamstress,

121
00:08:16,267 --> 00:08:21,687
but I need money to pay for the guild membership fees and such.

122
00:08:27,157 --> 00:08:28,307
The way I see it,

123
00:08:28,307 --> 00:08:33,327
you could make more money from guarding merchants than from herding sheep.

124
00:08:33,327 --> 00:08:35,447
I bet it's hard to find unclaimed fields.

125
00:08:36,167 --> 00:08:37,377
It is.

126
00:08:37,377 --> 00:08:41,547
There are many shepherds in every safe area.

127
00:08:42,587 --> 00:08:45,467
So all that's left are wolf-strewn fields, huh?

128
00:08:45,467 --> 00:08:46,297
Yes.

129
00:08:47,217 --> 00:08:49,257
Wolves sure can be a pain.

130
00:08:56,147 --> 00:08:58,597
And they're clever and sly, too!

131
00:08:59,107 --> 00:09:02,567
If I speak ill of them, they may hear, so...

132
00:09:03,777 --> 00:09:05,027
Indeed.

133
00:09:15,077 --> 00:09:19,377
I'm sorry for making you stop this early.

134
00:09:19,377 --> 00:09:25,047
It's no problem. I know that shepherds have to get to sleep before the sun goes down.

135
00:09:25,047 --> 00:09:28,297
I have to watch over the sheep throughout the night, so...

136
00:09:29,217 --> 00:09:36,307
When I look at their wool, I always wonder what kind of clothing it'll be made into.

137
00:09:37,097 --> 00:09:40,107
You do a remarkable job.

138
00:09:40,107 --> 00:09:41,647
I'm very impressed.

139
00:09:41,647 --> 00:09:43,437
You're flattering me.

140
00:09:43,437 --> 00:09:47,697
You should be in charge of more sheep, judging from your skills.

141
00:09:47,697 --> 00:09:51,697
No, it's only by God's blessings that I'm entrusted with even this many.

142
00:09:51,697 --> 00:09:54,367
A huge flock... I just couldn't...

143
00:09:54,367 --> 00:09:56,157
Your employer has no eye for skill.

144
00:09:57,287 --> 00:09:59,497
Maybe it's time for a change?

145
00:10:00,957 --> 00:10:04,087
No way. I couldn't possibly do that.

146
00:10:04,797 --> 00:10:09,877
Apologies. We merchants tend to think about things based on loss and profit.

147
00:10:11,097 --> 00:10:12,137
Um...

148
00:10:12,137 --> 00:10:12,927
Yes?

149
00:10:12,927 --> 00:10:16,307
Do people change their employers often?

150
00:10:16,677 --> 00:10:21,517
It's normal, if one is unsatisfied with one's terms of employment.

151
00:10:21,517 --> 00:10:23,317
Is that so?

152
00:10:24,067 --> 00:10:27,067
Pardon me for asking, but might your employer be the Church?

153
00:10:28,277 --> 00:10:31,067
It's just my merchant's intuition speaking.

154
00:10:31,617 --> 00:10:36,367
Yes, I'm tending to the sheep of a Church pastor.

155
00:10:36,697 --> 00:10:39,827
He's been very considerate to me as well.

156
00:10:42,627 --> 00:10:44,587
I take back what I said.

157
00:10:46,047 --> 00:10:52,207
Your wages may be low, but the Church will never cease to exist until God himself forsakes us.

158
00:10:52,757 --> 00:10:56,697
You'll never be out of work, and you'll always have something to eat.

159
00:10:57,387 --> 00:10:59,017
You're right.

160
00:11:00,097 --> 00:11:01,557
You're right.

161
00:11:01,557 --> 00:11:06,317
God never said anything against doing work on the side, though.

162
00:11:07,357 --> 00:11:14,687
When we arrive in Lubinheigen, I'll make sure to ask my fellow merchants whether they need a reliable escort.

163
00:11:14,997 --> 00:11:18,077
Really? I'd really appreciate it!

164
00:11:25,837 --> 00:11:27,797
Hard work, that.

165
00:11:28,097 --> 00:11:31,087
Daily care of one's tail is important.

166
00:11:33,057 --> 00:11:35,547
Oh, you meant the child.

167
00:11:35,547 --> 00:11:37,767
Her name is Norah Arendt.

168
00:11:43,307 --> 00:11:43,807
Hey!

169
00:11:46,767 --> 00:11:50,187
Look, I did ask for your approval.

170
00:11:50,987 --> 00:11:53,387
Can't even relax and groom my tail.

171
00:11:53,387 --> 00:11:54,687
Why couldn't you have done it in here?

172
00:11:55,947 --> 00:11:57,447
If I'd done it in here...

173
00:11:57,737 --> 00:11:59,287
If you did it here... what?

174
00:12:03,747 --> 00:12:06,627
You certainly seemed to enjoy your chat with her.

175
00:12:07,537 --> 00:12:08,747
With Norah?

176
00:12:08,747 --> 00:12:11,427
Who else would I be talking about? The dog and sheep?

177
00:12:12,717 --> 00:12:16,757
She wanted to talk. I didn't have any reason to refuse, did I?

178
00:12:17,297 --> 00:12:20,367
It's been a while since I had a real conversation with a normal girl.

179
00:12:20,967 --> 00:12:25,257
You couldn't even tell that she was uncomfortable speaking with you?

180
00:12:29,067 --> 00:12:31,067
Well, that's okay.

181
00:12:31,687 --> 00:12:36,067
If it was love at first sight, I wouldn't have the pleasure of seeing her fall for me.

182
00:12:39,577 --> 00:12:42,497
What do you think? Aren't I quite the smooth talker?

183
00:12:45,077 --> 00:12:48,457
It doesn't fit you! It doesn't fit you at all!

184
00:12:54,467 --> 00:12:56,467
You don't have to laugh so hard.

185
00:12:56,467 --> 00:12:57,517
Geez.

186
00:12:57,517 --> 00:12:59,347
It's hilarious!

187
00:13:02,637 --> 00:13:03,927
Are you done yet?

188
00:13:03,927 --> 00:13:07,887
Yes, that's quite an ace you had up your sleeve.

189
00:13:08,307 --> 00:13:11,647
Well, if your bad mood is gone, that's all that matters.

190
00:13:12,397 --> 00:13:15,397
Yes, it all seems so trivial now.

191
00:13:15,857 --> 00:13:18,137
It's like it was a gift from the child herself.

192
00:13:39,257 --> 00:13:40,847
Good morning.

193
00:13:41,637 --> 00:13:42,547
Nice to see you again.

194
00:13:42,547 --> 00:13:43,887
That's it.

195
00:13:45,017 --> 00:13:45,847
Thanks.

196
00:13:47,057 --> 00:13:48,517
Thanks, as always.

197
00:13:51,147 --> 00:13:52,557
You saved me a lot of trouble.

198
00:13:53,317 --> 00:13:58,187
It would have taken ten times as long to obtain transit documents if we had to sit through routine inspections.

199
00:13:58,657 --> 00:14:01,187
It's a benefit of being employed by the Church.

200
00:14:02,277 --> 00:14:05,197
Here's forty Trie, as promised.

201
00:14:06,327 --> 00:14:10,537
But if I exchange these silver coins, won't it come out to forty-five?

202
00:14:10,537 --> 00:14:13,207
Call it an investment by a greedy merchant.

203
00:14:13,207 --> 00:14:14,047
Investment?

204
00:14:14,757 --> 00:14:21,047
Now that I know such a skilled shepherd, I might come across an opportunity to turn a profit on wool sometime.

205
00:14:22,007 --> 00:14:23,547
Thank you very much.

206
00:14:24,347 --> 00:14:28,347
We'll be staying at the trading house of the Lohen Trading Union.

207
00:14:28,347 --> 00:14:31,977
Make sure you stop by before you head out to the fields with your sheep.

208
00:14:31,977 --> 00:14:35,277
I may be able to introduce you to a few merchants in need of security.

209
00:14:35,277 --> 00:14:36,567
Thank you very much.

210
00:14:37,437 --> 00:14:42,487
By the way, do you have to stay on the path we traveled on?

211
00:14:42,487 --> 00:14:46,567
No, I'm allowed to move to Kasrata, Poroson, and even Lamtra.

212
00:14:46,997 --> 00:14:48,077
Lamtra?

213
00:14:48,077 --> 00:14:49,617
Are you talking about...

214
00:14:49,997 --> 00:14:50,907
Yes.

215
00:14:51,327 --> 00:14:54,287
You don't travel on the roundabout official route, do you?

216
00:14:54,287 --> 00:14:56,787
I take the shortcut through the forest, of course.

217
00:14:57,167 --> 00:15:00,507
That eerie forest makes even the bravest of knights blanch.

218
00:15:00,507 --> 00:15:03,047
I have no worries as long as I'm with Enek.

219
00:15:03,547 --> 00:15:06,837
I daresay you'll have plenty of business, then.

220
00:15:07,557 --> 00:15:09,387
I look forward to it.

221
00:15:10,227 --> 00:15:12,967
The entrance for livestock is that way, so I'll excuse myself.

222
00:15:20,777 --> 00:15:24,097
All that's left to do now is go through customs

223
00:15:24,097 --> 00:15:28,577
and head to Lemerio Trading to sell the armor that we obtained thanks to you.

224
00:15:28,577 --> 00:15:31,987
We're <i>also</i> going to buy peaches preserved in honey with what we earn.

225
00:15:32,287 --> 00:15:33,917
Time to get a move on.

226
00:15:33,917 --> 00:15:35,837
Hey, don't ignore me!

227
00:15:36,417 --> 00:15:38,377
We can't buy any if they aren't selling any.

228
00:15:38,377 --> 00:15:40,587
Chances are they won't have it, you know.

229
00:15:40,587 --> 00:15:41,797
I know.

230
00:15:42,257 --> 00:15:43,887
Don't make a fuss if they don't.

231
00:15:43,887 --> 00:15:44,967
I'll do just that.

232
00:15:45,547 --> 00:15:46,597
I told you...

233
00:15:50,977 --> 00:15:52,017
What's that?

234
00:15:52,017 --> 00:15:54,977
It prevents enemies from entering during times of war.

235
00:15:54,977 --> 00:15:57,557
They use those holes to pour scalding oil on the enemy.

236
00:15:57,567 --> 00:16:00,187
This is more of a castle than a city.

237
00:16:04,237 --> 00:16:05,647
Letter of transit?

238
00:16:08,907 --> 00:16:10,197
From Poroson?

239
00:16:10,197 --> 00:16:11,497
What are you carrying?

240
00:16:11,497 --> 00:16:13,657
Twenty sets of armor.

241
00:16:13,997 --> 00:16:16,167
Armor from Poroson?

242
00:16:16,747 --> 00:16:21,077
Yes, I purchased them wholesale from Latparon Trading. Is something wrong?

243
00:16:24,887 --> 00:16:25,877
Well, all right.

244
00:16:26,507 --> 00:16:29,097
How will you pay the taxes? Cash or goods?

245
00:16:29,097 --> 00:16:30,637
Oh, with goods.

246
00:16:31,767 --> 00:16:33,687
That's a wise decision.

247
00:16:33,687 --> 00:16:35,887
Hand over two sets right over there.

248
00:16:36,647 --> 00:16:40,567
Is it that rare to make a wholesale purchase from Poroson?

249
00:16:40,567 --> 00:16:42,357
Not in my experience.

250
00:16:42,357 --> 00:16:43,647
It's quite the contrary.

251
00:16:46,617 --> 00:16:47,687
Here you go.

252
00:16:53,037 --> 00:16:54,037
You may pass.

253
00:16:56,037 --> 00:17:00,077
Bureaucrats will always be unpleasant people regardless of where you are.

254
00:17:00,957 --> 00:17:02,417
Didn't you notice?

255
00:17:02,417 --> 00:17:05,547
That civil servant scoffed at you.

256
00:17:06,087 --> 00:17:08,887
After seeing our pile of armor, he probably thought,

257
00:17:08,887 --> 00:17:13,247
"Don't act so high and mighty just because you're making money."

258
00:17:14,057 --> 00:17:17,757
I don't care what he thought. We were able to enter town without a hassle.

259
00:17:18,267 --> 00:17:20,817
Let's park our wagon and head to the market.

260
00:17:35,367 --> 00:17:36,447
Good morning.

261
00:17:37,367 --> 00:17:38,787
Good morning.

262
00:17:50,927 --> 00:17:52,807
Do you now understand?

263
00:17:55,307 --> 00:17:58,557
That hit the spot! Sir, one more!

264
00:17:58,557 --> 00:18:02,437
One beer coming up. You sure can hold your liquor, young lady!

265
00:18:02,437 --> 00:18:03,977
I've barely started!

266
00:18:05,687 --> 00:18:10,067
You've fallen for one who loves to spend money, but she's a real beauty.

267
00:18:10,067 --> 00:18:12,777
She'd be perfect if she didn't have a tail.

268
00:18:16,117 --> 00:18:19,447
The liquor is good and the people lively. 'Tis a good city, no?

269
00:18:20,207 --> 00:18:22,497
The liveliness comes at a price.

270
00:18:22,877 --> 00:18:25,757
Watch yourselves around knights or mercenaries, okay?

271
00:18:25,757 --> 00:18:27,757
A quarrel with them means a world of trouble.

272
00:18:27,757 --> 00:18:28,967
Here you go.

273
00:18:29,507 --> 00:18:31,427
You can count on me!

274
00:18:34,257 --> 00:18:35,927
Where are we going now?

275
00:18:35,927 --> 00:18:37,347
The trading house.

276
00:18:38,387 --> 00:18:41,057
Wait up. You have froth on the side of your mouth.

277
00:18:45,817 --> 00:18:46,937
Hey!

278
00:18:47,777 --> 00:18:48,687
Geez!

279
00:18:49,277 --> 00:18:51,277
Still...

280
00:18:51,737 --> 00:18:55,117
Why must you drag me along to this trading house with you?

281
00:18:55,117 --> 00:18:57,157
It's too dangerous to leave you alone.

282
00:18:58,367 --> 00:19:00,867
It's true. I am a bit too lovely to be left unattended!

283
00:19:00,867 --> 00:19:02,307
Not quite what I meant.

284
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:05,797
What if you get drunk and let your ears or tail show?

285
00:19:05,797 --> 00:19:10,677
I'd just grab you in my jaws, and we'd dash from the city.

286
00:19:10,677 --> 00:19:12,627
I can surely leap over those walls.

287
00:19:13,217 --> 00:19:17,887
Isn't there an old tale about a knight and a girl like that?

288
00:19:17,887 --> 00:19:20,557
The one where the knight carries the captive girl to safety?

289
00:19:20,557 --> 00:19:22,097
That's the one!

290
00:19:22,097 --> 00:19:27,437
Unlike the story, there's not a trace of romance in the idea of being carried away in a wolf's jaws.

291
00:19:27,437 --> 00:19:28,987
Forget it. No way.

292
00:19:29,817 --> 00:19:33,067
You aren't the sort that would look good getting rescued anyway.

293
00:19:34,447 --> 00:19:35,777
By the way,

294
00:19:36,787 --> 00:19:39,037
what is a trading house?

295
00:19:39,957 --> 00:19:42,787
Risk and accidents go hand in hand with business,

296
00:19:42,787 --> 00:19:45,377
and there's no one who will protect you from either one.

297
00:19:46,167 --> 00:19:48,377
Just as knights wear armor,

298
00:19:48,377 --> 00:19:52,257
we merchants protect ourselves by banding together.

299
00:19:52,837 --> 00:19:56,847
Where we're going is a branch office of merchants who share the same birthplace.

300
00:19:57,557 --> 00:20:00,057
This always brings me back!

301
00:20:00,057 --> 00:20:03,307
All of the buildings in my hometown look like this.

302
00:20:05,517 --> 00:20:10,277
It must be nice to have your home scattered across the land.

303
00:20:12,237 --> 00:20:15,657
Stay here while I take care of business.

304
00:20:15,657 --> 00:20:20,447
What? Are you not going to bring me in and brag about how lucky you are to your countrymen?

305
00:20:20,447 --> 00:20:24,577
I'll be done before you know it. If you wait nicely, I'll buy you some sweetbread.

306
00:20:25,127 --> 00:20:27,087
Don't treat me like a child!

307
00:20:27,087 --> 00:20:27,957
You don't want any?

308
00:20:28,627 --> 00:20:30,007
Of course I do.

309
00:20:45,147 --> 00:20:48,137
What are you doing here, you sad excuse of a merchant?

310
00:20:49,187 --> 00:20:53,147
Wandering around here at this hour... Cares not a whit for making money...

311
00:20:53,147 --> 00:20:55,697
You'd be better off as a thief!

312
00:20:55,697 --> 00:20:59,737
Great merchants earn their money without having to soil their shoes.

313
00:21:00,117 --> 00:21:03,117
The only stain is the ink upon their fingers.

314
00:21:03,867 --> 00:21:07,747
Running around the market all day is the sign of a third-rate merchant.

315
00:21:07,747 --> 00:21:08,917
Am I wrong?

316
00:21:10,127 --> 00:21:12,087
You've found yourself a way with words.

317
00:21:12,087 --> 00:21:15,257
Welcome back, my son!

318
00:21:17,297 --> 00:21:19,637
Please stop the "my son" nonsense.

319
00:21:20,597 --> 00:21:27,147
What are you saying? All in the Lohen Trading Union are my sons and daughters.

320
00:21:27,147 --> 00:21:32,437
I even know of all the times you wet your bedroll after we made camp.

321
00:21:33,107 --> 00:21:38,857
Or should I mention the time you and your friends stole money and snuck off to the brothel, scared shitless?

322
00:21:38,867 --> 00:21:41,367
All right! All right!

323
00:21:50,997 --> 00:21:54,047
Did a man called Lawrence come by?

324
00:21:55,757 --> 00:22:00,757
Lawrence? I haven't even seen a mouse these past few days.

325
00:22:01,347 --> 00:22:02,597
I see.

326
00:23:40,817 --> 00:23:44,977
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and Conspiracies."</i>

327
00:23:45,907 --> 00:23:49,997
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and Conspiracies."</i>

